<!-- $description Classes used with Phone1st for quick styling. -->
<!-- $url test/class.html -->
<!-- $post-image test/test-images/phone1st-class.webp -->
<!-- $css classes.css -->

<!-- @import includes-kit/_test-header -->

<div>
  <p class="text-center text-lg font-500 mb-3">Experimenting with <em>classes.</em></p>
    <p class="text-center mb-4">
      Phone1st uses the color palette from <strong>Tailwind css</strong>.</p>
      <p class="lh-6 mb-4">
      <strong>A mixin is used to generate all the classes</strong>. In the <em>class</em> folder the <em>_class-helpers.scss</em> imports all the partials as <em>maps</em> and with a <em>mixin</em> adds <em>breakpoints</em>, <em>colors</em> and <em>size </em> where needed.</p>
      <p class="mb-4">To add a <em>class</em> is simple you just add it to the <em>map partial</em>. In <em>development</em> the output file <em>style.css</em> in the <em>build</em> folder weighs about <em>82kb</em>. In <em>development</em> the mixin generates a lot of <em>classes</em>. In <em>production</em> the unused css styles should be purged and the file should come down to about <em>28kb</em>.
    </p>
    <p>You can take the <em>class utilities</em> as far as you like or you can easily remove them</p>
  <hr>
